{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:4bb01f0e95fa17e7","name":"Ugnaught Worker","source":{"id":"source:reference-4bb01f0e95fa17e7","title":"Ugnaught Worker","revision":19598,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:15:22Z","sha256":"89855d2ea3235c3931293f399391ebe0f153be15ea167a8baeee0ae29294ec52","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19598","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Ugnaught%20Worker&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-4bb01f0e95fa17e7","blocks":[{"tag":"table","children":["\n\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["This section was titled Ugnaught in its official source, but has been renamed to distinguish it from the similarly named \"",{"tag":"a","children":["Ugnaught"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ugnaught?action=edit&redlink=1"},".\""]}]},"\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["These natives of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gentes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gentes?action=edit&redlink=1"}," have long suffered various degrees of slavery. Their rugged build and aptitude for mechanics make them ideal industrial workers, but their lack of planetary defenses and military structure make them vulnerable to the more aggressive powers in the galaxy. Throughout history, different forces- both official governments and corporate entities as well as freelancing slavers- have raided ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gentes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gentes?action=edit&redlink=1"}," and exported entire communities of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ugnaughts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ugnaughts?action=edit&redlink=1"}," to industrial sites across the galaxy.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Ugnaughts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ugnaughts?action=edit&redlink=1"}," suffer under slavery during ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", too, as Separatist forces raid ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gentes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gentes?action=edit&redlink=1"}," and haul away thousands of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ugnaughts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ugnaughts?action=edit&redlink=1"}," to work in factories producing ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"},", weapons, and vessels, including the Droid foundries on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Geonosis"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Geonosis","referenceId":"reference:2f85e38b680a11c3"},". Many escape in the aftermath of battles and sieges, leaving the scarred worlds to establish independent enclaves. The floating Tibanna gas mining installations of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Bespin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Bespin","referenceId":"reference:9fbf56e3fbef483c"}," have long provided one of the few free havens for expatriate ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ugnaughts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ugnaughts?action=edit&redlink=1"},"; here they maintain both the mining machinery and the infrastructure facilities that keep the cities aloft. Over the years they have become valuable members of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Bespin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Bespin","referenceId":"reference:9fbf56e3fbef483c"}," populace.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Ugnaught Worker Statistics (CL 2)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Small Ugnaught ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 6\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":